7. She dislikes rail replacement buses and associates them with discomfort and illness. (Verbatim: "oh rail replacement buses i hate rail replacement buses i'd have got a bus then pain pain")
8. She has knowledge of UK HR practices and corporate culture, having been close to an HR employee. (Verbatim: "i was really good friends with the hr lady um at my one of the jobs i worked at and i just found it fascinating")
9. She is familiar with corporate jargon and passive-aggressive email language, which she finds amusing. (Verbatim: "corporate talk is actually hilarious like have you guys ever done like corporate talk like it'll be like as per my last email aka why didn't you read what i last said")
10. She has encountered workplace references that used euphemisms to criticize former employees. (Verbatim: "they were like a very interesting interesting and weird personality... this individual is very special") [end of text]



