1. She enjoys eating chicken nuggets and discovered they can be cooked in five minutes using an air fryer. (Verbatim: "i can make chicken nuggets in my air fryer in in in five minutes and i was like what excuse me what")

2. She has a fondness for smiley face-shaped potatoes, which she considers a “fancy” and mature food despite their playful appearance. (Verbatim: "i had these little potato smiles because you know i'm a really mature adult that has really mature food")

3. As a child, her parents refused to buy smiley face potatoes or Lunchables because they were seen as expensive and not cost-effective. (Verbatim: "my parents would never never get them because they're like why would we pay extra for food in the shape of like stuff when it's just food")

4. She never had Lunchables as a child due to their high cost, though she expresses a nostalgic desire to try them. (Verbatim: "i've never actually had a lunchable um because my parents said that it was it was it was very expensive and not very cost effective")

5. She recalls British school lunches being poor quality, especially after health reforms, and remembers one particularly disappointing watery pasta meal she saved bus money to buy. (Verbatim: "i remember i saved up my bus money to to buy it and i was so sad it was so it was so watery it was like the sad watery passed a pot")

6. Her school had a vending machine that only offered unappetizing healthy options like bruised fruit and exploding yogurts, which she found awful. (Verbatim: "they'd replaced everything in the vending machine with just random random healthy items so talking like a bottle of water")

7. She strongly dislikes liver and once refused to eat it for nearly four hours at the dinner table as a child. (Verbatim: "liver is something i absolutely cannot eat okay it was it was cooked for me once by my parents and honestly... i think it was like almost four hours i was sat there like i'm not eating it")

8. Her parents enforced a rule that she couldn’t leave the dinner table until she finished all her food, leading to prolonged standoffs. (Verbatim: "my parents would be like oh you can't leave you can't leave the dinner table until you finish all your food")

9. She values minimizing food waste and believes using the whole chicken, including bones and skin, is sensible and respectful to the animal. (Verbatim: "same dude it's it's like food waste like what you want to just throw it away like you killed that chicken mate eat it all")

10. She enjoys chicken skin and finds it delicious, contrasting with people who dismiss it as undesirable. (Verbatim: "i love chicken skin put a load of chicken skin in here that's delicious") [end of text]



1. She was a middle child and often felt forgotten. (Verbatim: "yo fellow middle child what up it's me also middle child middle child middle child heck yeah i was forgotten quite a bit um i was a middle child i was a middle child")

2. She was labeled the "smart child" in her family and faced high academic expectations. (Verbatim: "i was also the smart child um yeah yeah yeah yeah yeah yeah so it was more like oh we don't need to take care of her she takes care of herself")

3. Her parents expected her to get top grades but discouraged her from studying, preferring she do chores instead. (Verbatim: "they wanted me to get top grades but they didn't want me to to study which was the weirdest part they would rather i be cleaning like or doing chores")

4. She had a cousin of the same age, and their parents constantly compared them academically. (Verbatim: "i have so i have like a cousin that's like the same age as me... they'll be like oh let's pit these two up against each other and compare them constantly")

5. She disliked being made an example of by teachers and had difficult experiences with some educators. (Verbatim: "oh I hate it being made an example of yes I had a lot of mean teachers I'll be honest")

6. She struggled with attention and focus in school, often doodling or zoning out during class. (Verbatim: "i don't have a very big attention span so i used to doodle a lot um like a lot like i'd have my notebook and i would just doodle on it")

7. She sometimes zones out to the point of being mentally absent despite having her eyes open. (Verbatim: "my eyes are open but I'm not looking through them like does that make sense like the eyes are open but you're not you're not there you're just gone")

8. She found school and university lectures difficult due to her inability to focus as a listener. (Verbatim: "I'm not a listen learner okay okay like even at uni I just remember being sat there and be in my head I'd be like okay Ellie what are we gonna do today we're gonna listen to the professor")

9. She used to do other students' homework for them, viewing it as "free XP" like in a video game. (Verbatim: "i would do their homework... i considered it like a video game okay i wanted the free xp give me your homework")

10. She resented the generational mindset of enduring hardship and passing it on, vowing to break the cycle. (Verbatim: "i don't we must continue the generational trauma until until morale rises like like i don't understand gotta break that cycle i don't get it") [end of text]



1. She has had multiple close calls with traffic while crossing roads, including nearly being hit by cars five times in one 30-minute walk. (Verbatim: "i got almost run over five times that day like every single road i was like i was actually trying to safely cross the road i don't know how it kept happening")

2. She once walked home from Nando’s because she spent all her money on food and couldn’t afford the bus. (Verbatim: "i think at the time i was walking from nando's... i used all my money on the chicken and i don't have enough for the bus so i'm gonna walk")

3. She fell out of trees frequently as a child due to climbing and being clumsy. (Verbatim: "like i used to like climbing trees as a kid and i used to get stuck and i used to fall a lot because i'm quite clumsy")

4. She got stuck on top of a large metal container and had to jump down because she didn’t have her phone. (Verbatim: "i climbed on top of one of those um containers you know like the big big containers... and i got stuck and i didn't have my phone and i was there for like an hour and then i had to figure out how to like jump down")

5. She fell down three flights of stairs, slid all the way down, and was badly bruised but felt more confused than hurt at the time. (Verbatim: "the furthest i've fallen i accidentally um fell down some stairs but it was like three flights of stairs and i went all the way down... i think i had like adrenaline i didn't hurt and then i realized i was so bruised")

6. She slept on a top bunk bed without the bottom bunk and frequently rolled off it while sleeping. (Verbatim: "i had for a little bit while growing up and i like rolling around in my sleep... the amount of times i rolled off that bed was too many too many times")

7. She has a surprisingly high pain tolerance and tends to hide her pain to avoid bothering others. (Verbatim: "i've been told i have quite a high like surprisingly high pain tolerance... i'm pretty good at hiding said pain if that makes sense mostly because i don't want to be a bother")

8. She dissociates during scary experiences like roller coasters, becoming silent and mentally checking out. (Verbatim: "if you stick me on something scary like a zipline or roller coaster i go dead silent i just straight up dissociate from existence")

9. She went on several roller coasters at Fuji-Q Highland, including one with 3.1 g-force acceleration and another that reaches 130 km/h. (Verbatim: "i went on fujiyama it's supposed to be like it's certified as a one of the largest roller coasters with no overturns... the fujiyama one goes at 130 kilometers per hour")

10. She relates to cheetahs, describing herself as working at 0% or 100%—either completely inactive or working at extreme speed for short bursts. (Verbatim: "i resonate with cheetahs because like they're they're zero or 100 and that's how i work i'm either napping doing absolutely nothing rotting away or working at 100 at super speed") [end of text]



1. She attended university in England and studied a demanding course with over 10 modules, requiring extensive study. (Verbatim: "back in school in uni i would be classed as like overachiever... i had so many modules as well it wasn't even that i had half amount of modules i still had like like over 10 modules")

2. She struggled financially during university and could not afford to go out or attend trips. (Verbatim: "i can't afford it... i couldn't afford the third option i'll be honest um the third option there the party option that costs money alcohol is expensive")

3. She worked multiple jobs while studying at university to support herself. (Verbatim: "i didn't have a lot of money i was working like all these jobs i was trying to study")

4. She played League of Legends frequently during university as a way to cope or relax. (Verbatim: "i remember at uni i did have to study... but like my goodness it was it was a struggle... i played a lot of league")

5. She identifies as a procrastinator and believes working under pressure improves her performance. (Verbatim: "procrastination is a good skill because then you can deal with last minute issues... pressure makes diamonds okay")

6. She had a breakdown when she dropped her cottage pie on the floor, which symbolized her stress and hunger during university. (Verbatim: "i was on the floor like on my hands and knees next to this cottage pie in absolute shambles... crying like and then and then my um my housemate walked in")

7. She lived with nine other girls during her second year of university, who were wealthy and did not understand her financial limitations. (Verbatim: "this was second year uni i shared with we have nine other girls... the only issue was that they were all incredibly rich")

8. She felt isolated and misunderstood by her wealthy housemates when she couldn't afford an end-of-year trip to Greece. (Verbatim: "they wanted to go to greece or something... i can't afford to do that... they just thought i didn't want to go with them")

9. She does not come from a financially supportive family and cannot rely on her parents for money. (Verbatim: "i could call my parents right now and you could listen to them laugh like why didn't i just say that i couldn't afford it")

10. She finds comfort in flexibility and believes productive rest is important to avoid burnout. (Verbatim: "you can't work at like 200% all the time... productive rest is so real") [end of text]



1. She worked three jobs while struggling financially and supporting her family. (Verbatim: "i was working three jobs and stuff and starving but a lot of the money i was earning was going to my family")

2. Her parents do not understand financial hardship and believe that working hard always leads to financial success. (Verbatim: "they don't understand about the idea of not being able to afford something... they just it was like a missing link in their brain")

3. She grew up in a house with significant living difficulties, including a broken window that let in a constant breeze. (Verbatim: "i swear i remember being like um yo mother father my window's not windowing like at all i'll be honest um because if i hold my hand here like it's a breeze")

4. She attended university in England where she experienced group project challenges and advocated for herself with professors. (Verbatim: "i remember i went to the professor and i was like yo professor like these are the you i know you brought our grade down because these parts suck")

5. She successfully argued for a higher individual grade in a university group project due to unequal contributions. (Verbatim: "i got to okay i'm not paying for an expensive degree and not snitching")

6. She participated in academic research expos involving scientific poster presentations during university. (Verbatim: "we had to make a group scientific poster thing... these posters are massive and you have to like do certain parts")

7. She is aware of and acknowledges her own privileges despite facing financial struggles. (Verbatim: "i wouldn't say i was the most underprivileged kid like i know there were other kids that had things way worse than me so i still accept my privilege")

8. She finds it frustrating when wealthy people deny their privilege and claim to be working class. (Verbatim: "they'd be like no no no no no no i am most definitely working class and i'm like not with that extent heck you want me like you ain't ever seen a rat in your life")

9. She has a critical view of the UK student finance system, noting that most people never fully repay their loans. (Verbatim: "after 30 years the loan gets wiped it's like done gone... i would say yeah like heckin 99.9 percent of people won't pay it")

10. One of her university peers had a significant academic advantage because her father was a Cambridge professor in the same subject. (Verbatim: "one of the girls at my uni like her father was a professor at the university of cambridge and would help her with all her uni work") [end of text]



1. She has a strong dislike for sweat bees, which are harmless but swarm and are attracted to sweat. (Verbatim: "sweat bees my hacking but hated they're they're harmless but my god i hated them so much they swarmed me")

2. She was bitten excessively by gnats during a childhood school trip, causing her neck to swell and preventing her from joining a night walk. (Verbatim: "i got bitten by so many gnats that i had to like i wasn't allowed to go on the night walk because my neck started swelling")

3. During a school trip, she was left with a French class that spoke no English, and they watched *The SpongeBob Movie* together while she drank hot chocolate. (Verbatim: "they just dumped me with this random class of french people and we watched the spongebob movie... i was very cozy")

4. She has a monolingual background and does not speak any language other than English, which she attributes to her mother not teaching her. (Verbatim: "i'm a monolingual punk okay my mother never bothered to teach me anything")

5. She once traveled to a rainforest, where she had to drink large amounts of water and used hydration salts to stay properly hydrated. (Verbatim: "when i was yeah in the rainforest i had to drink so much i drank so much water while over there because you just sweat it all out")

6. She took malaria tablets during a trip, which she disliked. (Verbatim: "i had to take these malaria tablets and they suck")

7. She completed a master’s degree, during which a hornet lived in her room for an extended period before dying behind a chair. (Verbatim: "this was during my masters... i look behind a chair and and guess what i find in the corner on the floor i find its dead tired body")

8. She dislikes the experience of washing her hair after camping due to fear of bugs in damp, dark places. (Verbatim: "washing your hair after a camping trip was a horrifying experience oh my god oh my god it's like the scariest part is like because they like damp places")

9. She once accidentally ate chicken butt (chicken tail) at a street food stall in Asia and found it disgusting. (Verbatim: "i ate chicken butt and it was awful and i hated it and i don't like chicken butt and chicken butt tastes awful")

10. She has a fear of mosquitoes and gets bitten frequently, more than most people. (Verbatim: "i get bitten by mosquitoes quite a lot like like a lot a lot") [end of text]



1. She once unknowingly ate chicken butt from a street vendor. (Verbatim: "i asked my mother to read the sign... she was like yes chicken butt and i was like i don't want to eat chicken butt")
2. She enjoys trying adventurous foods like chicken feet and cow’s tongue but avoids spicy food. (Verbatim: "i do like to try and be adventurous with my food... the only thing i'm not adventurous on is spicy things")
3. She had two trips to America where she tried local food, including Costco hot dogs, and noticed her body reacting strongly to greasy food. (Verbatim: "when i went to america i was like i want to try american food... first trip i couldn't finish the costco hot dog second trip i did finish the costco hot dog")
4. She worked at a zoo in the past and often ended the day covered in animal poop, which made commuting home by bus embarrassing. (Verbatim: "i worked at the zoo... i was covered in it like it was awful... getting the bus when you absolutely stink sucks")
5. She is afraid of large flies, wasps, and spiders, and once avoided her own living room for days due to a wasp. (Verbatim: "i hate them i hate them i just i just hate them... i didn't enter my living room for like a few days after that")
6. As a child, she was terrified of spiders and would ask her parents to remove them, sometimes finding them missing and panicking. (Verbatim: "as a kid i struggled... where's the scariest spider because it'd be like on my bed or something")
7. She loves penguins, especially after seeing the penguin parade at Edinburgh Zoo, but finds them smelly due to their fish odor. (Verbatim: "they're so cute... penguins smell like fish if you're wondering how they smell")
8. She has a fear of mystery meat but acknowledges it has led her to enjoy unusual foods like chicken feet. (Verbatim: "i don't eat mystery mystery meat's not always bad like like mystery meat is how i got to try chicken feet")
9. She struggles with forgetting to eat, which may have contributed to losing weight despite consuming burgers. (Verbatim: "i keep forgetting to eat... i somehow lost weight i actually need to gain weight")
10. She cannot drive and relies on public transportation, which was particularly difficult when returning home smelling of animal waste. (Verbatim: "i can't drive so for me to get back home i'd have to get two buses") [end of text]



